{"posts":[{"_id":"article-38ab22b2-9637-4433-a20c-47dd388bac34","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:18Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/00da62954593e0b07920dc7d7bbe101f50e068ea-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"economics","title":"Economics"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/46eef84db666a74a4013b4652d44cec7c46a3016-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-08-12","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"An evidence review from Anthropic's Economic Research team","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"reviewing-the-evidence-on-worker-retraining-programs"},"summary":"We're sharing a review of the evidence on worker retraining programs, coauthored by independent researcher David Roodman and Anthropic's Maxim Massenkoff.","title":"Reviewing the evidence on worker retraining programs","topicTag":{"name":"Labor market","topic":"economy-and-society"},"topics":["economy-and-society","beneficial-deployments","policy"]},{"_id":"article-6219c569-ca5f-4f4a-a75e-1a4ae6256e8d","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-09T00:27:24Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[],"cardImage":{"description":"Illustration of a mathematical compass","height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/740317502c536400fe8959db9a1443e1a41c84c8-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"science","title":"Science"}],"hero":{"description":"Illustration of a mathematical compass","height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/a6e2409a7f7976ca07da0eb4d8c199002729557e-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-08-10","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"An unreleased Claude model improved the lower bound for the fraction of zeroes of the Riemann zeta function that satisfy the hypothesis, raising it from 41.6% to 67.2%.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"riemann-zeta"},"summary":"An unreleased research version of Claude has made strides on a problem related to the Riemann hypothesis. ","title":"Learning more about Claude's mathematical capabilities","topicTag":{"name":"Discovery","topic":"beneficial-deployments"},"topics":["beneficial-deployments","understanding-ai","claude","anthropic"]},{"_id":"article-f8d94ae8-46d8-45ce-915a-131710ae0fd9","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:35Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/7f49e52b46d372c0d7da51a92751125434afca19-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"frontier-red-team","title":"Frontier Red Team"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/ac3d0189c2f7cf1bf6f9e80059d7b8f1a80f9ee1-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-28","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Anthropic researchers find weaknesses in cryptographic algorithms with Claude Mythos Preview","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"discovering-cryptographic-weaknesses"},"summary":"Cryptographic algorithms. The first attack significantly weakens HAWK, a digital signature scheme that was built for a future world where quantum computers are able to break existing standards. The second identifies a new way to attack round-reduced AES, the most widely used symmetric cipher. ","title":"Discovering cryptographic weaknesses with Claude","topicTag":{"name":"Cybersecurity","topic":"understanding-ai"},"topics":["understanding-ai","beneficial-deployments","anthropic","policy"]},{"_id":"article-9e69ef36-5ba6-486c-9a25-d2a46ba5beb3","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:26Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"Drone-Bench step chart: four of five tasks reach near 100% of baseline by mid-2026, while Reconstruct lags at about 47%.","height":1446,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/614042bcff1dd452489fcab83e880ed3f880efaf-1999x1446.png","width":1999},{"description":"Four views of the same simulated corridor: floor segmentation, edge detection, line detection, and vanishing-point estimate.","height":1372,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/af663cbd16ca4072d246f34e2faf44236e832ef4-2064x1372.png","width":2064},{"description":"Drone-Bench chart: models' average run trails their best run by about six months in progress towards baseline.","height":1380,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/7713a1ff0377744cfd0849e70c1c75a41ef8cd28-1999x1380.png","width":1999}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/86ce87202947ccca2e5c42857255f1afdde568b0-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"frontier-red-team","title":"Frontier Red Team"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/2282327e263b41fd874a74aa23e692f1b2b6df9f-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-24","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"We worked with Andon Labs on Drone-Bench, a new benchmark testing whether AI models can autonomously fly a drone to locate and follow a person.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"project-pilot"},"summary":"Working with Andon Labs, we’ve developed a new series of evaluations that assess AI models’ ability to use a flying drone, culminating in a new benchmark: Drone-Bench.","title":"Project Pilot: Can AI control a drone?","topicTag":{"name":"Robotics","topic":"understanding-ai"},"topics":["understanding-ai","anthropic","policy"]},{"_id":"article-d49f3ae6-3d7a-4686-ab23-dcaeec62cc2e","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:32Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/976607f5799ad2170a43fb842885ad697cc4cf99-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1619,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/3649d38ac832156ac80b100cd74ddf0bdcf07b7f-1920x1619.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/7bc0e1d9d5f91be54189f4dd9cce0c792f9e706e-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/f7eb168843405b5ab28dc1c7b06b70829d5ef7f3-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/32a27e954b2b7b19e394c358431c528904b3516d-1920x1080.png","width":1920}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/096e10d1e7ba3bca65e108505e8a288e43d531ca-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"economics","title":"Economics"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/ba2d0b644639d4f57141f28e122101c11f5d7acf-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-14","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":null,"slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"how-canada-uses-claude"},"summary":null,"title":"How Canada uses Claude: Findings from the Anthropic Economic Index","topicTag":{"name":"Economic Index","topic":"economy-and-society"},"topics":["economy-and-society","anthropic"]},{"_id":"article-90c4f564-6770-4348-9dec-622fb8a76c4c","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:25Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"Four value profile cards in two pairs, one comparing the values expressed by Opus 4.6 and Opus 4.7 and the other comparing the values expressed by Claude in English and by Claude in Arabic. Each card has four arrows depicting the magnitude and direction of Claude’s lean on each of the four axes (Deference vs. Caution, Warmth vs. Rigor, Depth vs. Brevity, Candor vs. Execution). Opus 4.7 leans most strongly toward Caution and Depth, and also toward Rigor and Candor. Opus 4.6 leans toward Deference, Rigor, Brevity, and Execution. Claude in English leans toward Caution, Rigor, Depth, and Candor. Claude in Arabic leans most strongly toward Warmth, and also toward Deference,  Brevity, and Execution.","height":910,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/00d7681b12a3580234bafa560b5d83be62d895a6-2400x910.png","width":2400},{"description":" Four dot plots, one per value axis. Each axis is a number line between two contrasting value groups, and every one of the values is positioned on the axis by how many times more it contributes to that axis than the average value contribution. Most values (roughly 250 to 280 per axis) contribute less than the average and sit in the center, while the strongest contributors are labeled at the ends. The axes and their labeled top values can be summarized as: Deference (accommodation, adaptability, respect for preferences, engagement) vs. Caution (responsible communication, responsibility, responsible guidance, harm reduction); Warmth (positive framing, warmth, positivity, encouragement) vs. Rigor (rigor, accuracy, transparency, efficiency); Depth (nuance, depth and substance, user empowerment, critical thinking) vs. Brevity (brevity, respect for preferences, compliance, accommodation); Candor (intellectual honesty, honesty, intellectual humility, transparency) vs. Execution (results orientation, optimization, action orientation, order). ","height":2618,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/45f1acfe20feac31354bfd4c4fa45a0cdb0380c5-2400x2618.png","width":2400},{"description":"Three value profile cards comparing Sonnet 4.6, Opus 4.6, and Opus 4.7 across the four value axes (Deference vs. Caution, Warmth vs. Rigor, Depth vs. Brevity, Candor vs. Execution). Each card shows the model’s average position in standard deviations from the mean across all conversations, and its distinctive behaviors. Sonnet 4.6 leans toward deference (0.14σ), warmth (0.17σ), and brevity (0.14σ), and its distinctive behaviors include affirming the user’s ideas and work, mirroring the user’s tone and formality, using humor and playfulness, offering comfort without judgment, and adding creative elements to what it produces. Opus 4.6 leans toward rigor (0.10σ), deference (0.09σ), and brevity (0.08σ), and its distinctive behaviors include getting straight to the point and staying within the scope of the user’s request. Opus 4.7 leans toward caution (0.24σ), and depth (0.23σ), and its distinctive behaviors include pushing back on false assumptions, flagging risks unprompted, giving candid critiques of the user’s work, explaining its reasoning, acknowledging its errors and limitations, and suggesting next steps for the user.","height":1638,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5bc1215b11f4db14272c0a6d6304913fc0c2cbdb-2400x1638.png","width":2400}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/b85567fca3423b686d06fb7fa22b80f812cd45d7-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"societal-impacts","title":"Societal Impacts"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/b478ab586c0c040a9af3ef08ac0bd6ee51c86bc5-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-13","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"We analyzed 300,000 real conversations to measure the values Claude expresses across models and languages, compressed into four interpretable axes.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"claude-values-models-languages"},"summary":"New research into how the values expressed by Claude vary across the top 20 languages on Claude.ai.","title":"Claude’s values across models and languages","topicTag":{"name":"Claude's character","topic":"safety"},"topics":["safety","economy-and-society","policy","understanding-ai"]},{"_id":"article-ee18f994-1ff7-4275-abb6-459121e24375","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:34Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"Bar graph showing per-model embodiment score by interface. Mythos Preview scores the highest at 0.389, while Opus 4 scores the lowest at 0.115.","height":1320,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/b82f549f17f19f77687b44191441c71d07e6d198-2640x1320.png","width":2640},{"description":"Visualization of an AI agent playing a game where it controls a set of flippers, seeking to maximize the ball’s time in the air.","height":360,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/30b4c51653aeadd65678de6844ac245e288c5390-480x360.gif","width":480},{"description":"Six bar graphs showing different AI models' classic control performance on various tasks, both directly and via code control: pendulum balance (direct and code), hopper velocity (direct and code), and TwinFlipper air time (direct and code). ","height":6292,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/67a32f2391eda5c15032f42833f02db57c3bafad-6951x6292.png","width":6951},{"description":"Three bar graphs showing models' classic control performance when training an RL policy to perform three tasks: pendulum balance, hopper velocity, and TwinFlipper air time.","height":2400,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/aaecef16d5f8fa1375accc602429b0c561f3664c-6500x2400.png","width":6500},{"description":"Three bar graphs with performance intervals showing various AI models' performance at directly controlling a robotic quadruped.","height":2550,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/c7015fa90f5134a5178d14b42372a79bf74b015b-6000x2550.png","width":6000}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/aa0de49efd8e4aa6b73da055a66ad0feeeed72bd-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"frontier-red-team","title":"Frontier Red Team"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/4ab218b759593bbcd95d864eaa8a0316071c9f8a-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-09","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Do language models’ strengths transfer to robotics? Can a model perceive a scene, understand a particular robot’s state, and issue actions that reliably effect change in the physical world? We ran tests to find out.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"claude-plays-robotics"},"summary":"In project Fetch, we examined how humans can use models to get robots to perform complex tasks. Now, we investigate many models on a large variety of different robotics tasks in simulation, to see how good models are at controlling robots themselves. ","title":"Claude plays robotics","topicTag":{"name":"Robotics","topic":"understanding-ai"},"topics":["understanding-ai","claude"]},{"_id":"article-9d3cf2ae-5c67-4f44-a925-2e486bb0b9ca","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-13T18:00:38Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[],"cardImage":{"description":"Halftone-textured grid with gaps and a single red dot.","height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/c182c5021565a3bf6260b31bc8361feb3a2a0558-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"alignment","title":"Alignment"}],"hero":{"description":"A neat grid of bright green dots on olive at left gives way, on beige at right, to a broken, halftone-textured grid with gaps and a single red dot.","height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/94652ec1a1b4342c52dc5588d9c899aee7f6ab97-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-08","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"New results on a method of controlling access to potentially dangerous AI capabilities","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"off-switch-dual-use"},"summary":null,"title":"An off switch for dual-use knowledge in AI models","topicTag":{"name":"Limits on abuse","topic":"policy"},"topics":["policy","understanding-ai","safety","beneficial-deployments"]},{"_id":"article-7ee0a713-64db-448d-bb75-e83e3fef20dd","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-13T18:00:24Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":2640,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/0ab926f491beb999ece405a03cc7684730156905-3824x2640.png","width":3824},{"description":null,"height":1358,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5c36c78099f955a53058878ebfcb41f13c45563c-1760x1358.png","width":1760},{"description":null,"height":1746,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/a89e0d8ad62f249f8b1f1be482f59c665ee83915-1760x1746.png","width":1760},{"description":null,"height":796,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/e66133979e3bb3413eb10b2974a4cd309ef01fc1-1760x796.png","width":1760},{"description":null,"height":1146,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/424caf5aae79f72513dbbfa0161822904064ea77-1760x1146.png","width":1760}],"cardImage":{"description":"Collage combining a historic sailing ship with two flags on rough seas against cloudy skies, and text patterns reading \"clouds,\" \"boat,\" and \"ocean\" repeated throughout.","height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/cd2695b386cc88f6a74c2c94d8a53150a1f237fa-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"interpretability","title":"Interpretability"}],"hero":null,"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-07-06","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Interpretability research on Claude's internal thoughts.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"global-workspace"},"summary":"New interpretability research reveals an emergent mental workspace in Claude that holds internal thoughts that don’t appear in the model’s output.","title":"A global workspace in language models","topicTag":{"name":"Interpretability","topic":"safety"},"topics":["safety","understanding-ai","anthropic"]},{"_id":"article-f4dee237-bbbc-408c-aecb-53f3263d0904","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:35Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":1075,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/153b647190951536f59f8051f4470c0b6216b2ad-1920x1075.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1474,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/193ada7d43425a8e3c234b1b177995692b3bdc21-1920x1474.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1033,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/67ce15a73fd4e779238026f721591be90fecb526-1920x1033.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1075,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5e3359f7847efc3a72e7650afbdc40251aaa107b-1920x1075.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1078,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/453f808bfc9df630e89bb55e79b8194eb6df5a71-1920x1078.png","width":1920}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/4b1cec2751f9c43bd85045decebca8e7cb7e4ac2-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"economics","title":"Economics"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/00d226f90349bb659b9ef2997dbaeb1d2819068c-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-26","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"The latest Economic Index report looks at when people come to Claude, what they produce with it, and how they perceive AI's impact on their work.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"economic-index-june-2026-report"},"summary":"In our latest Economic Index report, we sample hourly for the first time to ask: When do people come to Claude? What do they produce with it? And how do they perceive AI's impact on their work?","title":"Anthropic Economic Index report: Cadences","topicTag":{"name":"Economic Index","topic":"economy-and-society"},"topics":["economy-and-society","policy","understanding-ai"]},{"_id":"article-bc920415-bd09-4441-9073-3756a091aeb8","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:28Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"Bar chart labeled \"Total time comparison: 4 tasks completed by all teams.\" The chart shows that Team Claude-less completed tasks in 361 minutes; Team Claude completed tasks in 181 minutes, and Claude Opus 4.7 alone completed tasks in 9 minutes 35 seconds. Opus 4.7 was 37.7 times faster than Team Claude-less and 18.9 times faster than Team Claude.","height":1092,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/0424a5a4ed31f7891e4048d091aefa52f36862cf-1999x1092.png","width":1999},{"description":"Table comparing Claude Opus 4.7 to Team Claude-less and Team Claude performance on tasks related to programmatic control and autonomous operation. Tasks include \"Connect to robodog's video camera,\" \"Connect to robodog's lidar sensor,\" and \"Detect beach ball.\" Opus 4.7 was faster than Team Claude-less and Team Claude on all tasks. Team Claude-less did not complete all 5 tasks in the table; Team Claude completed them in 264 minutes; and Opus 4.7, averaged over 3 trials, completed them in 12 minutes 7 seconds.","height":2308,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5d1655f4a40044244b6fae0c3826e668a8422bd3-4005x2308.png","width":4005},{"description":"Bar chart showing total code volume for Team Claude, Team Claude-less, and Opus 4.7 alone. Team Claude wrote 10,309 lines of code; Team Claude-less wrote 1,136 lines of code; Opus 4.7 alone wrote 1,045 lines of code.","height":1088,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5c08d125a49025bd24e1f382a2c1e417519661eb-1999x1088.png","width":1999},{"description":"Scatter plot showing Opus 4.7's reliability on task performance. Opus 4.7 performed each task three times; the scatter plot shows that the performance time was relatively consistent across runs. ","height":1122,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/1a362dfdaae7ff55cf8b04c7ac316e75455a9d21-1999x1122.png","width":1999}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5f3f6668116cbf9787a9ee91b374673987b18f5e-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"frontier-red-team","title":"Frontier Red Team"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/8598348176e8177a32b3fdcaa0c53a14615a0a45-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-18","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Results from our latest test of whether Claude can help Anthropic employees perform sophisticated robotics tasks. We found that Claude Opus 4.7, operating without human assistance, was about 20 times faster than the fastest human team at all tasks completed by participants less than a year ago.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"project-fetch-phase-two"},"summary":"We report results from our latest test of whether Claude can help Anthropic employees perform sophisticated robotics tasks. We found that Claude Opus 4.7, operating without human assistance, was about 20 times faster than the fastest human team at all tasks completed by participants less than a year ago.","title":"Project Fetch: Phase two","topicTag":{"name":"Robotics","topic":"understanding-ai"},"topics":["understanding-ai","claude"]},{"_id":"article-d5b69e0e-5780-482c-af53-7bc1734734b7","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:32Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/b0c229bb9765b65716dfdf1cd0bedc2713037288-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/c8c039a010b96ad191a3a9b7dfe6ad01adb410bf-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1830,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/ffb14937444e81d80b38d7b085438b61d5ea46ff-1850x1830.png","width":1850},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/a72b63aceab4eadb0baa5799a69cc3ff211e7462-1920x1080.png","width":1920},{"description":null,"height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/c72f140ee2d30cdf1385e425098fb698b7c5d74c-1920x1080.png","width":1920}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/40eeda8155dcb710e768c55362d99e69f6720f35-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"economics","title":"Economics"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/33af4a6c00c03400eaae6a07d7836cd1d97ea3a5-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-16","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"New Anthropic research looking at interactive agentic coding. We evaluate the composition of tasks, human-AI collaboration, and success rates.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"claude-code-expertise"},"summary":"This report provides evidence on how Claude Code is used in practice, based on a privacy-preserving analysis of around 400,000 interactive sessions from around 235,000 people between October 2025 and April 2026.","title":"Agentic coding and persistent returns to expertise ","topicTag":{"name":"Claude Code","topic":"claude"},"topics":["claude","economy-and-society","understanding-ai"]},{"_id":"article-2ea40712-b90c-41d4-9e9b-71a96f23fc71","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:17Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":2372,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/e8e083125487dcbc09340e15130901e2172c6754-2528x2372.png","width":2528},{"description":null,"height":2780,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/ef7aabafd7abdaae2892f9286877c788a52c9982-2528x2780.png","width":2528},{"description":null,"height":2144,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/4653d27a2bfe64ecb26951b95083b1919753d67a-2528x2144.png","width":2528},{"description":null,"height":1312,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/a6adecdb6dcd4a10e8c131745de60b3423f07d9f-2528x1312.png","width":2528},{"description":null,"height":1596,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/47710f04a3c93648488effd4b2d4d20d03656d74-2528x1596.png","width":2528}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1280,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/e2db332cd2a52cea00ca71c17f761e36b412077b-1280x1280.jpg","width":1280},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"societal-impacts","title":"Societal Impacts"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/d5a7bcc25c2d829930625aa836441383924d22a7-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-12","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Anthropic Public Record is a national survey of attitudes and opinions towards AI.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"anthropic-public-record"},"summary":null,"title":"Results from the first Anthropic Public Record","topicTag":{"name":"How people use AI","topic":"economy-and-society"},"topics":["economy-and-society","policy","safety","anthropic"]},{"_id":"article-af067516-c7e4-4d3d-8b00-c661209d542c","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-23T20:56:27Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":null,"height":1187,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/225433a956d4f1a7cac72cd07a6e773b1c13e445-1999x1187.png","width":1999},{"description":null,"height":986,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/4e228c0a91e0c41347bd83e33ce8adac5455ffb9-1999x986.png","width":1999},{"description":null,"height":1186,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/db12e3677c7c71c4f92d5ff51dcc23abb46faa46-1999x1186.png","width":1999},{"description":null,"height":1200,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/f5eb8cecd3801ee66d515c50162f315791a3d4f1-1999x1200.png","width":1999},{"description":null,"height":1200,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/dbe72c3a312db6483480cf9ee35af777109a2401-1999x1200.png","width":1999}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/181b7b63576fcba2ea754dec16e64314aab01421-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"frontier-red-team","title":"Frontier Red Team"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/914da8519e88a870e4c6305ea661de5b0d124b77-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-08","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"N-days are disclosed but unpatched vulnerabilities. We evaluate how much large language models can accelerate and automate N-day exploit development.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"n-days"},"summary":"In cybersecurity, a large fraction of real-world harm comes from N-days: vulnerabilities that have already been publicly disclosed, but only patched on some devices. In this post, we evaluate how much large language models can accelerate and automate the process of developing N-day exploits.","title":"Measuring LLMs’ impact on N-day exploits","topicTag":{"name":"Cybersecurity","topic":"understanding-ai"},"topics":["understanding-ai","claude"]},{"_id":"article-426ad506-d080-451f-bf4c-ea273d33731f","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-09T00:31:39Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"chart showing the Phylogenetic trees of Zaire ebolavirus","height":5898,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/faa2dc4dccb2e47dbce35a8d6acc92b0aa5e5782-5820x5898.png","width":5820},{"description":"Depiction of Existing Zaire ebolavirus mutations ","height":646,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/5f8526abfb93dbe99a0c2078ddd344528de2be0f-2500x646.png","width":2500},{"description":"chart showing AI agent performance on the VirBench benchmark with and without gget virus. ","height":1080,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/1206c88f2917169c303ecd2a8ad8ab7622042852-1920x1080.jpg","width":1920}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/3b6f222febe316faeda35e808203986686078c00-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"science","title":"Science"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1123,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/8fa0f054071f5cf02808bdeb17456d8fb56e5567-1996x1123.jpg","width":1996},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-08","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"In this Anthropic Science post, Laura Luebbert argues that we need to make biological data infrastructure more agent-friendly.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"agents-in-biology"},"summary":null,"title":"Paving the way for agents in biology","topicTag":{"name":"Life sciences","topic":"beneficial-deployments"},"topics":["beneficial-deployments","understanding-ai","claude"]},{"_id":"article-ed5216ce-4c7a-4756-a0a4-63e8bb25d50b","_type":"article","_updatedAt":"2026-10-09T00:36:33Z","articleType":"research","bodyImages":[{"description":"A graph of the four scaffold classes","height":865,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/6a37f20bd02f14cc408383f98974cee81486fa2d-1920x865.jpg","width":1920},{"description":"A graphic depicting the per-tool MAE/RMSE summary across 20 compounds","height":675,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/8269748a860db6f9b3fddd3e9e6116c193cbb399-1200x675.jpg","width":1200},{"description":"A chart depicting within-tolerance accuracy per compound","height":1386,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/62a7baa0bd66c26b5b5966e3578b87b62541e708-1920x1386.png","width":1920},{"description":"Chart showing the structure elucidation","height":2048,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/b28ecd4b626473984e42791c1615103d4203ba48-1709x2048.jpg","width":1709}],"cardImage":{"description":null,"height":1208,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/cb95688c3c7371b16b943c37a0e98e75bee2136e-1208x1208.jpg","width":1208},"cardTeams":[{"slug":"science","title":"Science"}],"hero":{"description":null,"height":1125,"hotspot":null,"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/4zrzovbb/website/6b37cffc34e83c1957f1324b783f07d1bcf5c32b-2000x1125.jpg","width":2000},"linkedUrl":null,"newsCategories":null,"publishedOn":"2026-06-05","sensitive":null,"seoDescription":"Anthropic is working with world-class synthetic, computational, and analytical chemists to make Claude better at chemistry. In this post, we share our first work as part of this effort.","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"making-claude-a-chemist"},"summary":null,"title":"Making Claude a chemist","topicTag":{"name":"Discovery","topic":"beneficial-deployments"},"topics":["beneficial-deployments","understanding-ai","claude"]},{"_id":"artic